 runtime's prompt hook is wired and whether Codex has approved it.\\n63: The delivery leg reports DEGRADED, never FAIL, when a prompt hook is missing or the Codex hook is unapproved, and names the repair.\\n64: It reports each leg as passing, skipped, degraded or failing.\\n65: For a failing leg, it names the runnable doctor command that repairs it.\\n66: The sk-git leg passes `--tool=<name>` for the AI tool running the command.\\n67: Its exit 3 (an unknown check or a gate saved off) is degraded, not failing.\\n68: After the legs, it shows the last session hop from the session-relaunch hop history.\\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 69]\",\"title\":\"read\",\"metadata\":{\"metadata\":{\"truncated\":true},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md, lines 59-68\\n59: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\\n60: \\n61: The workflow prints the doctor target list.\\n62: It then runs seven read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check, the advisor status probe with `--warm-only` and the embedder check, which ...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/logs/w2-T013.out:\n  Line 2: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794546160578,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2cb7c2a8ffeJgvonzMMJV44b8\",\"part\":{\"partID\":\"prt_1d34951660012E5ZYgnVGiqne5\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2cb7c2a8ffeJgvonzMMJV44b8\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1d34948d70010vaVPVYD4ho2CD\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"id\":\"call_da6672ec4b16486eb86ac8db\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/tasks.md\"},\"output\":\"Read file /Users/michelkerkm