{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794546441324,"sessionID":"ses_e2cb7c22dffeZNysJSTmWyN01Q","part":{"partID":"prt_1d34d98b5001141854OqjEbV3P","sessionID":"ses_e2cb7c22dffeZNysJSTmWyN01Q","messageID":"msg_1d34d4759001TnbFoIwVCj1JBw","type":"tool","id":"call_2c1cd33ca15f405f99041d34","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt","offset":14,"limit":55},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt, lines 14-68\n14: \n15: Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n16: \n17: | Command | What it checks |\n18: |---------|----------------|\n19: | `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the seven read-only setup legs |\n20: | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem, with the class and the reason on every line |\n21: | `/doctor:env list` | The documented environment switches and where each value comes from |\n22: | `/doctor:update` | Whether a newer spec-kit release is available (bare runs the read-only check) |\n23: | `/doctor:git setup` | Whether the sk-git install, hooks, trust and standards are live |\n24: | `/doctor:git hooks` | Which shipped git hook gates are on or off, and switching one |\n25: | `/doctor:git standards` | The commit, PR and branch rules in .sk-git/ |\n26: | `/doctor:sk-code setup` | The sk-code setup battery, with a repair command per failing leg |\n27: | `/doctor:sk-code quality` | The repository quality config the gate reads with its tools, errors and disabled hygiene rules, then creating `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` once |\n28: | `/doctor:ci report` | Lists every workflow with its switch state, trigger, filters and drift flags, read against the repository CI profile; `scaffold` and `toggle` are the confirmed action routes |\n29: | `/doctor:sk-skill check [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>]` | How far one skill, or the whole fleet, is from the Skilled format, row by row, with the repair for each finding |\n30: | `/doctor:sk-skill convert <name-or-path> [--dry-run]` | Moving one skill to the Skilled format: the plan, one yes per write, the backup, the write and the engine's undo block |\n31: | `/doctor:agents-md [check|embed|restore] [--json] [--root <dir>] [--dry-run]` | The root instruction file: which shipped sections are current, embedding the template over a printed plan and its digest, and putting one recorded run back |\n32: | `/doctor:speckit` | The generated trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep recipes |\n33: | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Whether each runtime's agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors match .skilled |\n34: | `/doctor:skill-advisor tune` | Advisor recommendation quality and scoring tuning |\n35: | `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` | Rebuilding the skill graph database |\n36: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-budget` | Skill description character budgets |\n37: | `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` | A parent skill hub's structure and registry |\n38: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-graph-freshness` | Drift between the compiled, SQLite and on-disk skill graph |\n39: | `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` | Whether each declared routing phrase reaches its hub |\n40: | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | Meaning matching for commands: whether the local embedder answers, what it costs, and the plan that pulls the model and starts the server after a yes |\n41: | `/doctor:deep-loop` | Deep-loop coverage graphs and convergence for research, review and council runs |\n42: | `/doctor:mcp` | Code Mode install and debug, its UTCP configuration and runtime registration |\n43: | `/doctor:install [--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json]` | Putting Skilled into your own project repo: the build check, what is already linked, and the ordered setup commands to run |\n44: | `/doctor:symlink [check|link|unlink] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | The framework links in a project repo: which runtime folders are linked, broken or missing, linking them over a printed plan and its digest, and undoing one recorded run |\n45: | `/doctor:overlay [status|apply|repin] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | A vendored Skilled tree's own overlays: which destinations are out of sync and why, then putting them back, capturing one live edit, or re-pinning the tree to a newer upstream commit over a staged plan, after one yes |\n46: \n47: ## 3. Per-Leg Result Table\n48: \n49: Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n50: \n51: | Leg | Command | Result | Repair |\n52: |-----|---------|--------|--------|\n53: | [leg] | [check-only command] | [PASS|FAIL|SKIP|DEGRADED|ERROR] | [the doctor command that repairs it or shows why, or none] |\n54: \n55: | Leg | Repair when it fails |\n56: |-----|----------------------|\n57: | sk-code | `/doctor:sk-code setup` |\n58: | sk-git | `/doctor:git setup` |\n59: | trigger-index | `/doctor:speckit` |\n60: | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n61: | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n62: | embedder | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` |\n63: | delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |\n64: \n65: ## 4. Result Templates\n66: \n67: ### Summary\n68: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 69]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt, lines 14-68\n14: \n15: Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n16: \n17: | Command | What it checks |\n18: |---------|----------------|\n19: | `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the seven read-only setup legs |\n20: | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem, with the class and the reason on every line |\n21: | `/doctor:env list` | The documented environment switches and where each value comes from |\n22: | `/doctor:update` | Whether a newer spec-kit release is available (bare runs the read-only check) |\n23: | `/doctor:git setup` | Whether the sk-git install, hooks, trust and standards are live |\n24: | `/doctor:git hooks` | Which shipped git hook gates are on or off, and switching one |\n25: | `/doctor:git standards` | The commit, PR and branch rules in .sk-git/ |\n26: | `/doctor:sk-code setup` | The sk-code setup battery, with a repair command per failing leg |\n27: | `/doctor:sk-code quality` | The repository quality config the gate reads with its tools, errors and disabled hygiene rules, then creating `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` once |\n28: | `/doctor:ci report` | Lists every workflow with its switch state, trigger, filters and drift flags, read against the repository CI profile; `scaffold` and `toggle` are the confirmed action routes |\n29: | `/doctor:sk-skill check [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>]` | How far one skill, or the whole fleet, is from the Skilled format, row by row, with the repair for each finding |\n30: | `/doctor:sk-skill convert <name-or-path> [--dry-run]` | Moving one skill to the Skilled format: the plan, one yes per write, the backup, the write and the engine's undo block |\n31: | `/doctor:agents-md [check|embed|restore] [--json] [--root <dir>] [--dry-run]` | The root instruction file: which shipped sections are current, embedding the template over a printed plan and its digest, and putting one recorded run back |\n32: | `/doctor:speckit` | The generated trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep recipes |\n33: | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Whether each runtime's agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors match .skilled |\n34: | `/doctor:skill-advisor tune` | Advisor recommendation quality and scoring tuning |\n35: | `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` | Rebuilding the skill graph database |\n36: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-budget` | Skill description character budgets |\n37: | `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` | A parent skill hub's structure and registry |\n38: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-graph-freshness` | Drift between the compiled, SQLite and on-disk skill graph |\n39: | `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` | Whether each declared routing phrase reaches its hub |\n40: | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | Meaning matching for commands: whether the local embedder answers, what it costs, and the plan that pulls the model and starts the server after a yes |\n41: | `/doctor:deep-loop` | Deep-loop coverage graphs and convergence for research, review and council runs |\n42: | `/doctor:mcp` | Code Mode install and debug, its UTCP configuration and runtime registration |\n43: | `/doctor:install [--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json]` | Putting Skilled into your own project repo: the build check, what is already linked, and the ordered setup commands to run |\n44: | `/doctor:symlink [check|link|unlink] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | The framework links in a project repo: which runtime folders are linked, broken or missing, linking them over a printed plan and its digest, and undoing one recorded run |\n45: | `/doctor:overlay [status|apply|repin] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | A vendored Skilled tree's own overlays: which destinations are out of sync and why, then putting them back, capturing one live edit, or re-pinning the tree to a newer upstream commit over a staged plan, after one yes |\n46: \n47: ## 3. Per-Leg Result Table\n48: \n49: Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n50: \n51: | Leg | Command | Result | Repair |\n52: |-----|---------|--------|--------|\n53: | [leg] | [check-only command] | [PASS|FAIL|SKIP|DEGRADED|ERROR] | [the doctor command that repairs it or shows why, or none] |\n54: \n55: | Leg | Repair when it fails |\n56: |-----|----------------------|\n57: | sk-code | `/doctor:sk-code setup` |\n58: | sk-git | `/doctor:git setup` |\n59: | trigger-index | `/doctor:speckit` |\n60: | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n61: | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n62: | embedder | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` |\n63: | delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |\n64: \n65: ## 4. Result Templates\n66: \n67: ### Summary\n68: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 69]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\",\"offset\":14,\"limit\":55}"},"time":{"start":1794546440373,"end":1794546441324}}}}
