r line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |\n \n ## 4. Result Templates\n \n@@ -104,6 +105,7 @@ STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n | The advisor leg reports DEGRADED | Exit 0 has `data.freshness` other than `live`. The skill graph is not live. Run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n | The sk-git leg reports DEGRADED | No sk-git check failed, but one is unknown or a gate is saved off. Run `/doctor:git setup` to see which. On a runtime the battery cannot name, the AI-tool check stays unknown |\n | The trigger-index leg reports stale documents | Run `/doctor:speckit` to see which documents are stale |\n+| The delivery leg reports DEGRADED | A runtime cannot receive the advisor brief. Run the repair the leg names, then rerun /doctor:setup. The install still works without it |\n | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n \n End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\nindex b1f789aae3..257b64487b 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\n@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n \n | Command | What it checks |\n |---------|----------------|\n-| `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the six read-only setup legs |\n+| `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the seven read-only setup legs |\n | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem, with the class and the reason on every line |\n | `/doctor:env list` | The documented environment switches and where each value comes from |\n | `/doctor:update` | Whether a newer spec-kit release is available (bare runs the read-only check) |\n@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@ Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n | embedder | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` |\n+| delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |\n \n ## 4. Result Templates\n \n@@ -104,6 +105,7 @@ STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n | The advisor leg reports DEGRADED | Exit 0 has `data.freshness` other than `live`. The skill graph is not live. Run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n | The sk-git leg reports DEGRADED | No sk-git check failed, but one is unknown or a gate is saved off. Run `/doctor:git setup` to see which. On a runtime the battery cannot name, the AI-tool check stays unknown |\n | The trigger-index leg reports stale documents | Run `/doctor:speckit` to see which documents are stale |\n+| The delivery leg reports DEGRADED | A runtime cannot receive the advisor brief. Run the repair the leg names, then rerun /doctor:setup. The install still works without it |\n | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n \n End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794546440784,"end":1794546441433}}}}
